  <page>
    <title>Kindness</title>
    <id>246043</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41895546</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-02T12:59:30Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>JGF Wilks</username>
        <id>740658</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>changed link: St Paul</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Wiktionarypar|kindness}}
{{Wikiquotepar|kindness}}
{{otheruses2|Kindness}}
'''Kindness''' is the act or the state of [[charity|charitable]] behaviour to other people.  It is considered to be one of the [[Knightly Virtues]], and is a recognized [[value]] in many cultures and religions (see [[ethics in religion]]).  It is considered to be one of the [[seven virtues]], specifically the one of the Seven Contrary Virtues (direct opposites of the [[seven deadly sins]]) that is the direct opposite to [[envy]]&lt;ref&gt;{{web reference|url=http://deadlysins.com/virtues.html|title=Contrary, Heavenly, and Cardinal Virtues|work=7 Deadly Sins|date=2005-11-22}}&lt;/ref&gt;.

According to book two of [[Aristotle]]'s ''Rhetoric'' it is one of the [[emotion]]s (see [[list of emotions]]), which is defined as being &quot;helpfulness towards some one in need, not in return for anything, nor for the advantage of the helper himself, but for that of the person helped&quot;&lt;ref&gt;{{web reference|url=http://www.public.iastate.edu/~honeyl/Rhetoric/rhet2-7.html|title=Kindness|author=Aristotle (translated by Lee Honeycutt)|work=Rhetoric, book 2, chapter 7|date=2005-11-22}}
&lt;/ref&gt;.

[[Paul of Tarsus|Paul]] defines [[love]] as being `patient and kind...` ([[I Corinthians]]) 

One of the four [[caryatid]]s on the [[Wallace fountain]]s in [[Paris]] represents kindness.
{{culture-stub}}

== References ==
&lt;references/&gt;

== Further reading ==

* {{cite journal|volume=12-07 No:139|year=July 1998|author=RABBI-UL-AWWAL|title=What is Kindness to Parents?|journal=Islamic Voice|url=http://www.islamicvoice.com/july.98/hadith.htm}}
* {{web reference|url=http://www.islamonline.net/English/introducingislam/society/Neighborhoods/article02.shtml|title=Kindness to a Non-Muslim Neighbor: Tips for Interaction|author=El-Sayed M. Amin|work=Society|publisher=Islam Online|date=2005-11-22}}</text>
    </revision>
